{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, increase only the training-frequency input-feature amplitude from 0.04 to 0.08: scale visible item vectors by 1+0.08*tanh(z), using the existing standardized log1p training counts. Keep padding and mask scales unchanged and checkpoint the feature buffer. Stronger frequency cues may improve context reliability. Preserve embeddings, topology, readout, loss and optimizer.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, reduce only the tied normalized item-embedding radius multiplier from 0.8 to 0.65, retaining width 64 and input/output tying. A smaller radius may regularize catalog representations and reduce overconfident masked-item predictions. Keep frequency features, attention, history, loss temperature and optimizer fixed; use the same radius in training and prediction.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, add 0.05*mean(softplus((negative_score-positive_score)/0.8)) to the existing temperature-0.8 masked-item cross-entropy. Compute both scores at masked positions using the existing sampled negatives and tied embeddings. This may improve candidate separation while retaining full-catalog supervision. Keep sampling, architecture, features, optimizer and training schedule fixed.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, widen each bidirectional Transformer block's feed-forward intermediate dimension from 2*hidden_units to 3*hidden_units, retaining GELU, two attention blocks, existing heads and residual structure. Additional nonlinear capacity may capture item-context interactions without enlarging embeddings. Preserve features, masked-target training, appended-mask readout, loss and optimizer; ensure predictor construction matches checkpoint shapes."
}
